# Files that a test compares byte for byte are content, not text.
#
# Git for Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default, and that is
# what the CI runner uses, so a golden file with no rule here arrives with CRLF
# line endings while the code it is compared against emits LF. The test then
# fails printing two documents that render identically in a log — which is how
# this was found, and is worth one line to prevent.
**/testdata/** -text
